   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Write the Cartesian coordinates in terms of \\( \\theta \\): \\( x = r\\cos\\theta = \\left(\\theta\\right)\\cos\\theta \\) and \\( y = r\\sin\\theta = \\left(\\theta\\right)\\sin\\theta \\). At \\( \\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\), \\( r = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            "Pi",
            4
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Differentiate each product with respect to \\( \\theta \\): \\( \\frac{dx}{d\\theta} = \\frac{dr}{d\\theta}\\cos\\theta - r\\sin\\theta \\) and \\( \\frac{dy}{d\\theta} = \\frac{dr}{d\\theta}\\sin\\theta + r\\cos\\theta \\), where \\( \\frac{dr}{d\\theta} = 1 \\), which is \\( 1 \\) at \\( \\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\).",
         "mathjson": 1
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At \\( \\theta = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\): \\( \\frac{dx}{d\\theta} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(4 - \\pi\\right)}{8} \\) and \\( \\frac{dy}{d\\theta} = \\frac{\\sqrt{2} \\left(\\pi + 4\\right)}{8} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Multiply",
               [
                  "Sqrt",
                  2
               ],
               [
                  "Add",
                  "Pi",
                  4
               ]
            ],
            8
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The slope is \\( \\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{dy/d\\theta}{dx/d\\theta} = \\frac{\\pi + 4}{4 - \\pi} \\).",
